{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit built-in uniform priors for `sigma_a`, `sigma_b`, and `sigma_y`. These parameters already had finite bounds `[0, 100]` in the original Stan program, so the added `uniform(0, 100)` statements make the implicit bounded uniform priors explicit for SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. No data changes were made.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_groups;
  int<lower=0> n_scenarios;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_groups> group_id;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_scenarios> scenario_id;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_groups] a;
  vector[n_scenarios] b;
  real mu_a;
  real mu_b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[group_id[i]] + b[scenario_id[i]];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a ~ normal(10 * mu_a, sigma_a);

  mu_b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_b ~ uniform(0, 100);
  b ~ normal(10 * mu_b, sigma_b);

  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"group_id":[2,3,2],"n_groups":3,"n_scenarios":3,"scenario_id":[3,1,3],"y":[2.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
